(1) Transactions specified in Article 66 of Law No. 25/2019 (Income Tax Act);

(2) Transactions specified in Article 67 of Law No. 25/2019 (Income Tax Act);

(3) Among transactions governed by Law No. 10/2011 (Goods and Services Tax Act), transactions supplying goods or services to related parties;

(4) Transactions specified in item (5) of subsection (b) of Article 19 of Law No. 10/2011 (Goods and Services Tax Act).

3. Adding the following subsection after subsection (q-1) of Article 44 of the said Law.

44. (q-2) Notwithstanding subsections (q) and (q-1) of this Article, where the result of the amount determined by MIRA is a reduction in the amount of loss that may be deducted in a future accounting period under Law No. 25/2019 (Income Tax Act), no amount shall be required to be paid to MIRA in order to appeal that case in relation to the extent of that reduction in loss.

